{"abstract":"What we understand and choose as heritage is a question rooted in our individual and collective notions of identity and feelings of community. Critical heritage studies highlight the links between heritage and recognition, emotions, and the everyday lives of people and communities. We introduce a methodology for a digitally facilitated and participatory study of place-based community heritage. Inspired by Participatory Data Design and Photovoice methodologies, the Urban Belonging App enables participants to communicate phenomenological aspects of urban spaces by sharing, signifying, and evaluating pictures of familiar places in the city. A quali-quantitative analysis of the app’s data best exploits its multi-dimensionality: the characteristic of being both countable and measurable and semantically rich and relational. The case study illustrates how the methodology is used to study community heritage in an exploratory and descriptive way. Most valued and recognised heritage places, as well as less conventional understandings of heritage in Urbino, Italy, are identified. Two participants show how heritage differently embeds with everyday experiences, memories, and feelings of community. Its adaptability and ability to capture the contested and phenomenological nature of heritage and to operationalise complex definitions of community qualify the methodology to enable systematic research on bottom-up, situated heritage values.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pernarella, Marco","Madsen, Anders Koed"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-726094"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Pernarella, Marco"],"keyword":["Digital Methods","Participatory Design","Quali quantitative methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"urbino belonging exploring place based community heritage with digital amp participatory methods","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85164680697&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We would like to thank the following people, without whom this research would not have been possible. A special thanks to professors Anders Blok and Kristoffer Albris, for their valuable supervision to the MSc project from which this article originates. The IIS Raffaello Institute, the S. Girolamo Library administration, the Municipality of Urbino, Casa di Raffaello, Galleria Nazionale delle Marche, and Il Ducato for their support in communicating the project, as well as all those helping us spreading the voice. A special thanks to all the people most dear to us, who offered emotional support along the way. More than anyone else, we would like to thank all participants to the project, for their time, contribution, and energy."],"id":"S01-000.00-726094","identifier":[{"id":"85164680697","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a0ee8165-a34e-49f1-9a77-b02287a99669"],"keyword":["Heritage studies","community heritage","digital methods","participatory design","quali-quantitative methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D1C5DD0B89F74E71A245BC77BA3B2129"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, The Techno-Anthropology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, MASSHINE","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"pernarellapau","last":"Pernarella","name":"Pernarella, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"koedmadsenpau","last":"Koed Madsen","locid":"831b8679-0727-4ab6-b217-7e7bf47fbc63","name":"Madsen, Anders Koed","name_org":"Koed Madsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-2842-4908","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/13527258.2023.2231909","issn":["13527258","14703610"],"issn_org":["13527258"],"issue":"9","journal":"International Journal of Heritage Studies","pages":"939-960","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Heritage Studies","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164680697"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a0ee8165-a34e-49f1-9a77-b02287a99669"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Urbino belonging : Exploring place-based community heritage with digital &amp; participatory methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-726094","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
